WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:06.089
♪ (ROCK MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:11.428
Stay where you are, Smith.

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:15.849
I knew it was fucking
too good to be true.

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:18.101
Fuck! Fuck! Ah, fuck.

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:20.061
Fuck!

00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:24.482
Hey, everyone.
My name is Peacemaker

00:00:24.566 --> 00:00:25.775
and if it wasn't clear
by the outfit,

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.653
I am a genuine superhero
and protector of peace.

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:30.530
And I am Agent Emilia Harcourt.

00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:33.241
I'm here to provide
a factual account

00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:35.493
of Christopher Smith's history
with our agency

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:37.620
because we know
that he won't be doing that.

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:39.956
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:48.173
This whole thing kicked off
when Amanda Waller came to me

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:51.342
and asked me to lead
a super team to save the world.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.136
Close. Not exactly.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.054
The aforementioned super team
was comprised

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.849
of highly dangerous prisoners
serving time at Belle Reve,

00:00:57.932 --> 00:00:58.767
Smith included.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:01.519
For the duration of the mission,
I was in the communications hub

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:03.772
with John Economos
and Amanda Waller.

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:05.648
Smith was not the leader.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:09.986
Robert DuBois, aka Bloodsport,
was put in charge of team two.

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:10.945
Thank God.

00:01:11.029 --> 00:01:12.280
PEACEMAKER:
 My team was the real team.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.325
Team one were a bunch of losers,
disloyal and scared shitless.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.202
I think there was even
a fucking ferret or something.

00:01:17.285 --> 00:01:21.206
He was a weasel, but yes,
team one was a decoy,

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:23.082
sacrificed
for the larger mission.

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:24.918
That's not to say my team
didn't have its challenges,

00:01:25.001 --> 00:01:28.588
the biggest challenge being this
jackass with a stupid accent

00:01:28.671 --> 00:01:30.048
whose biggest accomplishment
was figuring out

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:31.883
how to hide a flame thrower
in his scuba suit.

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:33.802
Yeah, it was
a dick measuring contest

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:37.263
between Smith and DuBois
from moment one.

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:39.766
The exact number of friendlies
they took out is...

00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:41.100
still confidential.

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:42.560
Fuck that guy!
We can check the tape

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:43.978
and see who took out
more guerrillas--

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:46.356
soldier guerrillas,
not monkey gorillas.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.776
Okay, monkeys
would have been better.

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:51.861
You killed allies.

00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:54.239
I'm not saying
you should kill monkeys.

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:56.991
I don't want you to--
please don't go kill monkeys.

00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:59.077
Okay? Don't confuse me here.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.912
Anyway, we reach our target,

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:03.706
a lab called Guggenheim
or Heineken or something.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.041
EMILIA HARCOURT: Jötunheim.

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:06.835
(DRAWN OUT) Jötunheim.

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:10.296
PEACEMAKER: And inside,
we uncovered this alien starfish
 that was captured in space.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.757
And this starfish, by the way,
can control minds.

00:02:12.841 --> 00:02:15.093
Pretty fucking dangerous weapon
if you ask me.

00:02:15.552 --> 00:02:17.554
Unfortunately, Flag went rogue.

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:21.349
PEACEMAKER:
Rick Flag thought the truth was
 more important than peace.

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:22.600
I can't let you do that,
Colonel.

00:02:22.684 --> 00:02:23.560
Excuse me?

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.644
Let me be clear.

00:02:24.936 --> 00:02:27.689
Nothing is more important
than peace!

00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:30.066
Am I happy about what I did?
No.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.361
Peacemaker, what a joke.

00:02:35.238 --> 00:02:36.656
PEACEMAKER:
Then Mr. Micro-bullet shoots me

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:39.450
and a building fucking falls
on me, and lights out!

00:02:40.785 --> 00:02:42.453
I wake up in the hospital
three months later

00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:44.998
and I'm being asked
to save the world... again.

00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:47.125
Yeah, obviously we didn't have
a lot of options.

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:49.210
I'm pretty sure we would have
chosen anyone else

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:50.837
if we had the chance.

00:02:51.462 --> 00:02:53.756
But the world really is
in imminent danger,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.593
so let's just hope that
Smith can step up to the plate.

00:02:56.926 --> 00:02:58.636
I can step up
to any plate you got.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.681
I fuckin' love baseball,
American as apple pie.

00:03:02.098 --> 00:03:04.267
So the new mission is codenamed
Project Butterfly.

00:03:04.475 --> 00:03:07.228
I'll tell you right now,
if there's a Mothra about to be
unleashed on the world,

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:09.272
I will rip off
its giant ass wings

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.942
and fry its body with a massive
fucking magnifying glass!

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.654
That is not what
Project Butterfly is, okay?!

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:18.698
I mean,
they can't all be kaijus!

00:03:19.115 --> 00:03:22.619
Are we good here?
We have a lot of work to do.

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:26.122
Always fucking around, man.

00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:30.960
♪ (ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

